 "title": "Two-apart one-sided additive paths compose at recurring lags at every ring size",
 "subject": "Paths of rings joined by shared contacts, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law",
 "conclusion": "In four-ring paths with rule 60 or 102 on each ring and the middle contacts two apart, every contact binds both its rings at every lag at every ring size, and the last contact binds the end rings exactly where C(T - 3, m) is odd, m = 2, s - 2 or 2s - 6. By Lucas' theorem these lags recur, so all 64 families compose at recurring lags at every size, and at every lag none do.",
